These parameters lay out a standard limit-cycle scenario. The value of nu_kin here, 0.264, corresponds to a temperature of 249.2 K, assuming h_layer=0.37 (a prismatic facet)

&GI
   sigma0 = 20
   sigma0_units = 'percent'
   sigmaI_corner = 22
   sigmaI_corner_units = 'percent'
   c_r = 0.2
   c_r_units = 'percent'
   nu_kin = 0.264
   nu_kin_units = '1/microsecond'
   t_eq = 1.5
   t_eq_units = 'microsecond'
   nx_crystal = 501 
   Nbar = 1
   Nstar = .1
   h_layer = 0.37
   h_layer_units = 'nanometer'
   D = 0.0002
   D_units = 'micrometer^2/microsecond'
   L = 50
   L_units = 'micrometer'   
   d2Ntot_dx2_threshold = 10000
   d2Ntot_dx2_threshold_units = '1/micrometer^2'
/ 

&RT
   runtime = 300
   runtime_units = 'ms'
   ntimes = 50
   odemethod = 'RK45' 
   verbose = 0
/

Notes: 
Limit cycle is achieved after about 200 ms
Possible values for odemethod include RK45, BDF, RK23, DOP853, LSODA, and Radau
